1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,880
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

2
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:12,860
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

3
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:15,640
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

4
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:18,560
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,610
[Yoo Dohyun]

6
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,230
[Cho Chanhyeon]

7
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:39,930
[Ko Gyeol]

8
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:44,890
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

9
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,890
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers. Viewer discretion is advised.]

10
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,970
Everyone is willing to provide testimony,

11
00:00:57,970 --> 00:00:59,970
but no one wants to testify in court.

12
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,690
They're all afraid of being implicated.

13
00:01:04,129 --> 00:01:06,280
I've found the borrowed-name companies,

14
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,000
but they all have figurehead bosses.

15
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:12,190
There's no direct connection to the boss.

16
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:15,400
I've also gone through
the company's internal documents,

17
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,440
but the books are suspiciously clean.

18
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:19,570
Boss's name doesn't appear anywhere.

19
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,480
Everything is signed by Lee Won.

20
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,100
We can't turn the tables with just this.

21
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:25,550
These are all just signs.

22
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,850
[You have to sing, Hanyul.]

23
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,500
You have to sing,

24
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:45,910
Hanyul.

25
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,900
Run away with me.

26
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:52,979
What?

27
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:55,250
I said let's run away together—

28
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:57,380
to somewhere far away.

29
00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:00,750
To a place where no one can find us.

30
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,560
Your birthday?

31
00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:45,410
The last few digits of your phone number?

32
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:55,260
It must be related to you.

33
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:06,000
What?

34
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:08,130
What was it?

35
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,950
My debut date.

36
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:14,550
Lee Won is really something.

37
00:03:23,730 --> 00:03:25,050
But why are we here?

38
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:28,440
I thought there might be
something helpful here.

39
00:03:37,410 --> 00:03:40,280
True, Lee Won is definitely
not a simple guy.

40
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:45,630
There must be some evidence
hidden behind this.

41
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:50,460
But he couldn't do anything
in front of the boss.

42
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:53,110
Could it be that they have
something on him?

43
00:03:53,329 --> 00:03:57,100
It seems he's turning himself in
to take all the blame.

44
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,430
Why?

45
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:02,570
Why did he do that?

46
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,060
Do you have any clues?

47
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:25,760
[Collateral Contract]

48
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:25,610
Found it.

49
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,340
Collateral contract?

50
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:38,040
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

51
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:47,409
Hey, are you two out?

52
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,260
Yes.

53
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,360
Where are you?

54
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,760
Hanyul and I came to Lee Won's house.

55
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,760
Lee Won's house? Seriously.

56
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:55,800
We did find something, though.

57
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,700
What? Did you get anything?

58
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,710
Not anything
to completely turn the tables.

59
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:00,800
What is it?

60
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:02,970
But we can try some other way.

61
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,250
Damn it, what is it?

62
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,120
We found a special contract.

63
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:07,460
Contract?

64
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,370
I'm going to the Chairman's office
to look for a similar contract.

65
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,640
Okay, I got it.

66
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:19,640
Before Lee Hanyul comes of age,

67
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:23,140
Lee Won will repay all of Lee Hanyul's
debts and interest on his behalf.

68
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,540
During this period,

69
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:29,100
the creditor waives all personal
and legal rights over Lee Hanyul.

70
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,140
Come here.

71
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,400
Let me go!

72
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:37,570
Hey, you go.

73
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,400
Hurry up and go!

74
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:40,610
Mom.

75
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:42,159
Mom!

76
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,159
Mom!

77
00:05:43,430 --> 00:05:44,990
Don't ever come back.

78
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,540
That person back then was you.

79
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:59,950
If Lee Hanyul does not return
after coming of age,

80
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,330
500 times the interest
will be added to the original debt,

81
00:06:02,330 --> 00:06:04,010
and all debts

82
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:06,930
will be repaid by Lee Won himself

83
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,390
in full.

84
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:11,750
[Signature: Lee Won]

85
00:06:12,650 --> 00:06:14,230
Why on earth?

86
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:30,960
[A child abandoned
by his parents for just some money]

87
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:30,730
A child abandoned
by his parents for just some money...

88
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,690
A child who looked so much like me

89
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:40,750
when I was crying alone as a kid.

90
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:48,140
I was curious

91
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,840
if you could live a different life
from me

92
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,720
escaping this place.

93
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:59,040
Since I couldn't be saved,

94
00:06:59,170 --> 00:07:01,270
I thought I could at least
live a different life

95
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:03,550
through you.

96
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:17,740
That day,

97
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:21,840
I heard your singing for the first time.

98
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:25,460
And for the first time,

99
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,550
I had something I wanted to do.

100
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:32,150
I wanted to write songs

101
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,400
for you.

102
00:07:39,770 --> 00:07:42,710
To me, who was already trapped
in the gutter,

103
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:45,380
this dream was too whimsical—

104
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:48,330
something I didn't deserve to have.

105
00:08:01,670 --> 00:08:03,180
Where are you, rascal?

106
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:04,420
Get back here.

107
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:05,670
Yes, understood.

108
00:08:06,210 --> 00:08:07,060
Yes.

109
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:33,890
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

110
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:35,700
-You have to sing, Hanyul.
-You have to sing, Hanyul.

111
00:08:33,929 --> 00:08:36,880
[You have to sing, Hanyul.]

112
00:09:09,410 --> 00:09:10,890
Using young children as collateral,

113
00:09:10,890 --> 00:09:13,500
the so-called "child collateral loan" syndicate,
which illegally lent hundreds of millions of won,

114
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:17,570
has been arrested by the prosecution.

115
00:09:17,150 --> 00:09:22,740
[Defaulting parents; Forced placement into criminal syndicates;
Trained as organization members]

116
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:21,070
It is reported that after
forcibly taking custody of young children

117
00:09:21,070 --> 00:09:23,150
from parents unable to pay their debts,

118
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:25,650
they would forcibly entrust them
to criminal syndicates

119
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:29,610
to train them as gang members
for future criminal offenses.

120
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,980
These bastards are worse than animals.

121
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:37,030
They should be punished down
all their generations.

122
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,650
Shockingly,

123
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,010
this illegal organization

124
00:09:40,010 --> 00:09:43,250
belongs to the same company
as the entertainment agency

125
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:48,310
that recently caused an uproar over
a tens-of-billions-of-won money laundering case.

126
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:50,700
But Hanyul,

127
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:53,330
if it weren't for Won,

128
00:09:53,450 --> 00:09:57,380
you'd be holding a knife right now
instead of a microphone.

129
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:04,070
Also, Won sent a message,
so don't worry too much.

130
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:09,770
Speaking of which, Lee Won will
probably be locked up for a whole year.

131
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:12,950
Herod, you brat...

132
00:10:13,210 --> 00:10:16,590
Why do you sound so happy
and not worried at all?

133
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,570
I am worried.

134
00:10:18,710 --> 00:10:19,650
You brat.

135
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:24,820
A sincere voice
should come from the heart.

136
00:10:25,070 --> 00:10:27,390
I won't be able to sing anymore anyway.

137
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,100
Whose fault is that?

138
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:32,130
Who told you to be so despicable
as to steal someone else's song?

139
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:33,130
Hanyul,

140
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:35,080
do you want to sign
directly with our company?

141
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,140
What?

142
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,000
Isn't that piggybacking on his success?

143
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,230
That won't do.

144
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:43,580
You know that people
who just retired from the front lines

145
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,640
are more sensitive to trends, right?

146
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,280
Hanyul,

147
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:49,550
don't overthink it, just go with me...

148
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,930
You brat, you criminal.

149
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:53,630
Believe it or not,
I'll give you a karate chop.

150
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:54,700
Hanyul, you choose.

151
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,100
Who do you want to go with?

152
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,450
I just want to sing.

153
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,580
I want to sing.

154
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:09,730
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

155
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,490
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

156
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:23,190
my heart...

157
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:31,030
Herod, are you really
not going to sing anymore?

158
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:33,500
I just feel like this isn't right.

159
00:11:33,770 --> 00:11:35,910
You've practiced so much.

160
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:38,160
How can I have the nerve
to sing this song?

161
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:39,630
There too?

162
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:43,020
I'm leaving.

163
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:46,660
Hey, Herod.

164
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:48,870
Why?

165
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:51,490
Why not use that nice practice room

166
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:53,290
and insist on coming here to practice?

167
00:11:53,290 --> 00:11:54,240
Seriously.

168
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,850
Is the practice going well?

169
00:11:59,850 --> 00:12:01,200
Yeah, I guess.

170
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:04,270
Time flies so fast.

171
00:12:04,970 --> 00:12:07,780
Hanyul's concert is less than a week away.

172
00:12:08,150 --> 00:12:09,550
I mean, what rookie singer

173
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:12,030
would hold a concert
right after their official debut?

174
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:14,360
How many seats does that venue have again?

175
00:12:14,970 --> 00:12:16,900
Lee Won is really going overboard.

176
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:19,200
Brat.

177
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:23,080
The pre-released
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" was a hit.

178
00:12:23,190 --> 00:12:24,850
They say he even has a fan club.

179
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:27,290
Right, the fan club is called

180
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:28,220
Yulmu-cha—

181
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,840
no, oxblood soup (Seonjit-guk).

182
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:31,340
It's called Melody (Seonyul).

183
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:33,560
Right, I know. I know.

184
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:35,820
I also know the fans' nickname. It's...

185
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:36,680
Seasoned Salt.

186
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:37,750
Seasoning.

187
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,790
It's Sugar.

188
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:42,730
Brat, how do you know so much?

189
00:12:42,890 --> 00:12:44,540
He's a fan of Hanyul.

190
00:12:47,790 --> 00:12:48,890
All right.

191
00:12:49,550 --> 00:12:51,050
Then let's listen to this song.

192
00:12:51,050 --> 00:12:52,180
Composed by Adolph.

193
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,330
Sung by Lee Hanyul and Herod.

194
00:12:53,330 --> 00:12:55,930
Title, "Sound of Dawn."

195
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:57,370
Drop the beat!

196
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:02,780
I can't sing it.

197
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:04,940
Brat.

198
00:13:05,130 --> 00:13:07,010
You can't or don't want to sing?

199
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,870
Who would want to see me back on stage

200
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:12,460
singing the song I stole from a friend?

201
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:13,840
Don't you think?

202
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:23,490
For me.

203
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:28,780
Sing it for me, Herod.

204
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:32,280
We were too young back then—

205
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,040
too immature.

206
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:37,830
Things went completely differently
than we expected.

207
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:43,460
I don't want to waste
any more time on hatred.

208
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:47,060
So let's just look forward.

209
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:50,350
Don't look back, just look forward.

210
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:54,140
The song you took from me,

211
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,880
you can give it back to me.

212
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,380
You guys sing it.

213
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,860
You guys finish it.

214
00:14:30,610 --> 00:14:33,030
If you're listening,

215
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:36,500
please come back just once.

216
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:43,490
I'm still living in that dawn.

217
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,940
Today, I

218
00:14:46,210 --> 00:14:49,460
still cross the dawn,

219
00:14:51,490 --> 00:14:57,540
to call out to you once more.

220
00:15:02,350 --> 00:15:04,200
Thank you all.

221
00:15:08,890 --> 00:15:10,480
I used to

222
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,790
deeply hate

223
00:15:14,970 --> 00:15:17,330
my voice

224
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,470
and myself.

225
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,940
So I chose to run away.

226
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:27,120
I tried hard to erase myself.

227
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,000
Later, I met a group of great friends.

228
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,380
They made me realize

229
00:15:31,770 --> 00:15:33,670
that it's okay to run away.

230
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:35,810
And that I can choose to run away.

231
00:15:37,150 --> 00:15:39,630
As long as I come back.

232
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:45,810
The one who saved me from the world...

233
00:15:50,090 --> 00:15:52,550
who made me step out
of my own little world...

234
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,820
and the one who is by my side right now...

235
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:59,780
I'm making you
participate in Super Singer's audition.

236
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:00,620
Honey water.

237
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,520
You did nothing wrong.

238
00:16:08,590 --> 00:16:09,950
It was all you.

239
00:16:17,450 --> 00:16:20,550
The sound of it dropping

240
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:23,870
makes me care for some reason.

241
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:27,410
The moment you looked at me and smiled,

242
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,520
time stopped.

243
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:35,060
All the sunlight on
the hem of your uniform,

244
00:16:35,210 --> 00:16:38,830
the faint smile in your pocket.

245
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:41,920
I somehow called your name,

246
00:16:42,090 --> 00:16:45,470
and the breeze answered.

247
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:50,330
It was just an ordinary day,

248
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:54,310
but I don't know why it's so clear.

249
00:16:54,690 --> 00:17:00,830
I still remember the moment
I suddenly looked at you.

250
00:17:02,710 --> 00:17:06,210
Those unspoken feelings

251
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:10,510
melted in my mouth,

252
00:17:10,650 --> 00:17:17,480
disappearing piece by piece,
making the memory sweeter.

253
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:20,470
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

254
00:17:20,690 --> 00:17:24,329
my heart broke.

255
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:28,690
My mouth is full of

256
00:17:28,890 --> 00:17:33,150
the season named after you.

257
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:36,100
I thought even if it faded a little,

258
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:39,780
it wouldn't matter.

259
00:17:39,930 --> 00:17:43,240
But why do I still act like this?

260
00:17:43,370 --> 00:17:47,720
I long for you to stay sweet.

261
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:52,220
Leaning in a corner of the playground,

262
00:17:52,410 --> 00:17:56,470
it's like that song
is only for you and me.

263
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:59,760
Even if time takes everything away,

264
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:02,930
only that fragrance remains.

265
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:07,790
I tried to say I'm fine and smile,

266
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:12,380
but actually, I'm not.

267
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:15,160
Since the day I lost you,

268
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:18,370
the season stopped.

269
00:18:20,210 --> 00:18:23,710
Those unspoken feelings

270
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:27,870
melted in my mouth,

271
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:34,840
disappearing piece by piece,
making the memory sweeter.

272
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:38,030
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

273
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:41,570
my heart broke.

274
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:46,210
My mouth is full of

275
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:50,360
the season named after you.

276
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,420
I thought even if it faded a little,

277
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:57,230
it wouldn't matter.

278
00:18:57,440 --> 00:19:00,710
But why do I still act like this?

279
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:04,810
I long for you to stay sweet.

280
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:10,950
If one day we have
the chance to meet again,

281
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:14,930
will you smile as if
nothing ever happened?

282
00:19:15,050 --> 00:19:19,100
I hope at least this time, I can say it—

283
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:22,410
tell you

284
00:19:22,650 --> 00:19:25,500
all my feelings.

285
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:28,340
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

286
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:32,120
the world stopped.

287
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,300
Just like the day you smiled,

288
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:40,800
time also stopped.

289
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:47,490
Everything is at the end
of your white feelings.

290
00:19:47,650 --> 00:19:54,690
I'm still going to call out to you
like this.

291
00:19:54,710 --> 00:19:58,560
Still, still.

292
00:20:02,770 --> 00:20:06,400
Still, that sound of the sugar cube
is still here.

293
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:22,090
I was upset.

294
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:24,660
Hmm?

295
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:26,440
What do you mean?

296
00:20:28,070 --> 00:20:30,070
That you left without saying a word.

297
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:31,890
If I told you,

298
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:34,040
would you have let me go?

299
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,810
No, I wouldn't.

300
00:20:37,850 --> 00:20:40,770
But at least...
I wouldn't have let you be alone.

301
00:20:41,370 --> 00:20:42,660
I know.

302
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,010
That's why I left secretly.

303
00:20:45,730 --> 00:20:46,790
Tsk.

304
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:48,700
Hey.

305
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:52,630
I didn't even get to apologize
to you properly.

306
00:20:53,810 --> 00:20:55,550
Nor thank you, either.

307
00:20:55,990 --> 00:20:58,170
You were trapped there because of me—

308
00:20:58,470 --> 00:21:00,760
under his control
for the rest of your life,

309
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,050
only able to take his orders.

310
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:06,500
No.

311
00:21:09,530 --> 00:21:12,160
Thanks to you,
I found something I wanted to do.

312
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:15,790
I always hoped the songs you sang

313
00:21:15,970 --> 00:21:19,710
could be written by me.

314
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:23,130
If it weren't for you,

315
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:26,070
I probably would have been
a punk my whole life.

316
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,210
Tsk.

317
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:32,750
Don't just disappear like that ever again.

318
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,540
You too.

319
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:35,750
Mm.

320
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:36,920
Pinky swear.

321
00:21:37,090 --> 00:21:38,290
Pinky swear.

322
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:41,770
We're even now, one to one.

323
00:21:41,770 --> 00:21:43,780
Yeah, we're even.

324
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:44,950
So...

325
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:48,640
I'll be keeping an eye on you
for the rest of your life.

326
00:21:56,770 --> 00:21:58,830
Then I might as well go back to prison.

327
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,360
Hey...

328
00:22:00,470 --> 00:22:03,670
Even as a joke, you're not allowed
to say things like this.

329
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:36,180
[Thank you for your continuous love for "The Sound of Sugar Cubes"]
["The Sound of Sugar Cubes"]
